# The lexer example: read a source file named on the command line, split it
# into tokens located by line and column, write the token list to a file whose
# name is the source's name with `.tokens` added, and print a summary.
#
#   cd docs/refined-examples/lexer
#   python ../../../semanticscript/compiler/refined run . -- lexer-sample.txt
#
# The program may read and write only files in the working directory whose
# names start with `lexer-`. The path comes from the command line, so the
# scope is checked when the file is opened (D-38): any other path stops the
# program before the file is touched.

lexer is project
lexer purpose "Tokenize a source file named on the command line and write its token list"
lexer target console
lexer version "0.1.0"
lexer language refined 1
lexer standardLibrary 1
lexer allows read process.arguments none
lexer allows write console.stdout none
lexer allows write console.stderr none
lexer allows read fs.files "lexer-*"
lexer allows write fs.files "lexer-*"
lexer requires none
lexer includesModule lexer
lexer includesModule lexfile
lexer entry lexfile.main
